content.p:
The allegation in count 1 is one of a conspiracy to breach the provisions of section 1(1)(c) of the Official Secrets Act 1911 (the 1911 Act

 The 1911 Act was repealed on 20 December 2023 by the National Security Act 2023 (the 2023 Act): see  section 100(1), Sch. 18 para. 1 (with section 97) of the 2023 Act; and S.I. 2023/1272 reg. 2(f) (with reg.3).  
	      ) contrary to section 1(1) of the 1977 Act. The particulars of count 1 (as amended 

In his ruling, the judge said the particulars would need to be amended to exclude a reference to “calculated to or might be”, and this has now been done.
	      ) now allege that the defendants “between the 30th day of August 2020 and the 8th day of February 2023 conspired together and with Jan Marsalek and others unknown to obtain, collect, record, publish or communicate documents or information which was intended to be directly or indirectly useful to an enemy for a purpose prejudicial to the safety and interests of the State.”
